<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>4th August</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Its Time</B> <P>
<font size="3">


The past few weeks have really been a great test of my patience. Since the killing of Coirnav, Wudan has regained access to the Plane of Time. I would like to thank each member, init, guest, and especially the leaders on accomplishing what no one thought would be possible.  <P>

Along the way we picked up some decent stuff while outside of Planes of Power~  <P>

<img  src="http://www.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/deathwrap_of_rites.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/jagged_onyx_staff.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/rageshale_of_bolstering.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/shale_shoulderpads.jpg" > <P>

Loot is always nice : ) <P>

We still plan on recruiting, so if you have high play time and love to raid just about everyday look myself or other officers in game. Please ensure you meet our requirements and have zero KoS issues with other guilds before applying. <P>

Again grats Wudan on re-entry to PoTime. <P>

- Ealill <P>

</tr>




<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>3rd June</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Full steam ahead!</B> <P>
<font size="3">


Ahhhh. Its very satisfing to see the guild doing so well in the current EQ climate. With more heavy
hitting guids quitting EQ, its becomming more and more difficult to get a crew of good new
fresh faces AND keep the interest of the old hands.<P>

<img  src="http://www.somethingpositive.net/ads/bannerad4.jpg" align="right"> 

I'm very glad to see that Eaill and the current crew of dedicated officers are molding the 
current crop of recuits very well. Wudan raid disipline was always one of our strongest points
and I'm glad to see that its being maintained if not even improved on, as Wudan reflags to ensure
new applicants are able to experience the Elemental planes flag raids, as well as gain access
to the elemental planes for xping and AAing to the max.<P>

For all those people who find xping a little slow sometimes.. why not visit our new sponsor! You
two can find the love of your life with online multiplayer gaming......*wince*<P>

Finally, I've heard a lot of good things about our new applicants. I hope you all manage to maintain
the expectectations of your sponsors, and enjoy life on Wudan raids. Feel free to pass any comments
on to our officer team, or Ealill about your progress as a Wudan initiate. Remember.. the whole point
of this thing is to have fun, and get some chilled escape time from the real world. Enjoy, and no doubt
we'll see you all at Quarms corpse and on GoD raids soon. <P>

<BR>
<BR>
<BR>
<BR>

Needra

</tr>




<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>5th May</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>New hands at the helm</B> <P>
<font size="3">


Well Well.<P>
Its been a whirlwind past few months, and as a result Kadarx and I just haven't had much chance
to make time for any online games to any degree. I'd be breaking my own rules to sit in the leaders
chair when my play time is pretty low, so for a much needed change of pace the running of Wudan is 
being handed over to our top officers with Ealill taking the role of leader. (Thats O Glorious leader
to you).<P>

Theres a bunch of reasons while EQ has been struggling of late. Conquest had quite a good description
of the problems on their web site, when they made their last update. Basically if you play EQ at the
high end, you already know EXACTLY what the major problems are. Everyone does.<P>

The solution is to put people in charge who still love logging onto EQ _every_ day, and not just
for raids. People who have the time in their RL schedule to give a guild the online time it needs,
and those with good general raiding and game experience.<P>

As for Kadarx and Myself, we'll be around when time permits, and I suspect after the hectic summer
months have passed we may take the option to pursue a more active role for now. For the moment, tho
were gonna take a sunny hol and hang our swords up for a little while to grab some R&R while we
help the new kids plan a schedule for summer Wudan raids.<P>

Thanks to recent applicants/recruits who have been very patient while we hammer out the details
of all the changes, I suspect now we have an 'official' change of leadership you will see a very
swift return to active raids, on a nearly daily basis.<P>

With some luck the next update will be from Wudans leadership, with some details about the new
structure of command, any policy changes, and future ambitions. <P>

Lastly, seems GoD is getting a revamp. Could be _just_ in time to generate interest in the high
end game again :)<P>

</tr>






<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>28th Apr</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Wudan recuitment now open!</B> <P>
<font size="3">

Were looking for players with something special to offer to our guild, and the drive
to be a part of a well organised disciplined raiding guild. We expect our new members
to be level headed, mature and to have a love for online gaming.<P>

GoD has been a very 'challenging' expansion. At the high end its very, very slow
progress and pretty much tests a guilds character. We need people with the metal
to forge forward in new content, and face all the challenges EQ has to offer. <P>

At Wudan we try hard to ensure our new recruits benefit from being in the guild
as much as we benefit from having their sword or staff by our side. As part of
our dedication to new recruits, we'll be taking the opportunity to revisit a bunch
of content, beneficial to new members. <P>

We'll be flagging up all the old fun PoP content, to ensure new applicants are
ready to raid with us in the Elemental plans, Plane of Time AND Gates of Discord. As
a bonus we plan to continue to throw in the odd fun raid, for nostalgias sake, such 
as a few Emp kills, Vex Thall clearings.... and.. if you're very , very , very lucky...
Kadarx will come home drunk again... and drag the entire guild to North TOV to kill
Vulak at 4am in the morning, shouting at everyone in a drunken fashion, and pulling
the entire circuit of flurry drakes on the guild to 'test their metal'. *wince* <P>

Dont undertake this lightly. Being successful in EQ isn't easy right now. If you fancy
doing the 'odd' raid, Wudan aint for you. When the going gets tough, if you cant handle
it, Wudan aint for you. <P>

However, if you like FUN raids, tight raid discipline, mature guild ambiance... and most
of all... you really, really like to kill Dragons... then look us up!<P><BR>
	
Needra Malkuth<P>	

</tr>




